MiniClip import authorisation marker.

You do NOT need this file for MiniClip to keep its data next to the program — that is the
default: history, settings and logs go into the "data" folder beside MiniClip.exe.

This file does exactly one thing: it allows this copy to ADOPT data that already exists in
%LOCALAPPDATA%\MiniClip (history.json and settings.json), by copying it into "data" on the
next start. That is for people upgrading from an older version whose history still lives in
the user data directory.

It is a copy, never a move, and it never overwrites a history that "data" already holds.

Deleting this file stops the import from happening. It does not change where the data goes.
